I’d like to talk about a long journey I had with my family to Buon Ma Thuot about 4 years ago.

At that time, the COVID-19 pandemic was coming to an end, so we really wanted to go on a trip together to relax after being stuck at home for so long. We chose Buon Ma Thuot because none of us had been there before, and we had heard many good things about it, especially its coffee culture and peaceful atmosphere.

Since it’s quite far from where we lqive, around 350 kilometers away, my father decided to rent a 7-seater car, and it took us about eight hours to get there. Although it was a long drive, we actually enjoyed it because we could stop along the way to rest and enjoy the scenery.

We stayed there for three days and had a great time together. During the day, we visited different tourist attractions and took lots of photos, while in the evening, we tried local food and bought some souvenirs.

I really enjoyed this journey because it gave me a chance to spend quality time with my family, which doesn’t happen very often. Even though the trip was quite long, it was relaxing and memorable, and it’s definitely one of my favorite travel experiences.
